1. System Summary
The Smart Study Planner is a console-based Python application designed to help a student record, review, search and analyse study sessions during a semester. Each session stores the subject, topic covered, date/day label and duration in minutes. The application uses a menu-driven interface and separates its operations into clearly named functions.
The system also provides automatic session classification: Short sessions are below 30 minutes, Medium sessions are 30–90 minutes, and Long sessions are above 90 minutes. Study statistics calculate the total study time, study time per subject, the subject with the least study time, and the longest individual session.
2. Main Functions Implemented
Function
Purpose

main()
Controls the menu and keeps the application running until Save and exit is selected.

add_session()
Collects session details, validates duration and stores a dictionary in the sessions list.

classify_session(duration)
Classifies a duration as Short, Medium or Long.

view_sessions()
Displays all saved sessions in a formatted table.

search_by_subject()
Performs a case-insensitive subject search and calculates total time.

study_statistics()
Calculates overall hours, per-subject hours, weakest subject and longest session.

save_sessions()
Writes all sessions to study_log.txt.

load_sessions()
Loads existing records at startup and safely handles a missing file.

